yaml/code
description: One YAML document's content — a single value
- >
  A YAML code is one value — structured or scalar — with comments allowed around it. Structure
  is spelled by INDENTATION in block style, or by braces and brackets in flow style. yaml/code
  is a SUPERCLASS of [json/code](::language:01-Concretes_2:04-json_code) — every JSON code is
  valid YAML, arriving through the flow spellings:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  name: Julia
  age: 42
  pets:
    - cat
    - scorpion
  address: ~
- >
  See the subchapters below for the three parts:
- *: 00-yaml_structured
- *: 01-yaml_scalar
- *: 02-yaml_comment
- *..:..:04-json_code
